1
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Witness the incredible true story.

2
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:26,000
NYAD is a drama, history film directed by Elizabeth Chai Vasarhelyi.

3
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Athlete Diana Nyad sets out at 60 to achieve a nearly impossible lifelong dream: to
swim from Cuba to Florida across more than 100 miles of open ocean.

4
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Diana Nyad, played by Annette Bening.

5
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Bonnie Stoll, played by Jodie Foster.

6
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
John Bartlett, played by Rhys Ifans.

7
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Nico, played by Ethan Jones Romero.

8
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Luke Tipple, played by Luke Cosgrove.

9
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Angel Yanigahara, played by Jeena Yi.

10
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
Nyad is a 2023 American biographical sports drama film about swimmer Diana Nyad's
multiple attempts in the early 2010s to swim the Straits of Florida.

11
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
It is directed by Elizabeth Chai Vasarhelyi and Jimmy Chin (in their feature narrative film
directorial debut) and written by Julia Cox, based on Nyad's 2015 memoir Find a Way.

12
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
It stars Annette Bening as Nyad, with Jodie Foster and Rhys Ifans.

13
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
Nyad had its world premiere at the 50th Telluride
Film Festival on September 1, 2023.

14
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
Following its premiere at the 2023 Toronto International Film Festival, it was released in
select theaters on October 20, 2023, then streamed on Netflix on November 3.

15
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
Nyad received positive reviews from critics, with particular praise for the performances of Bening and Foster who both received nominations for Best Actress and
Supporting Actress, respectively, at the 96th Academy Awards, 29th Critics' Choice Awards, 81st Golden Globe Awards, and the 30th Screen Actors Guild Awards.

16
01:46:40,000 --> 01:46:46,000
The film explores themes of midlife crisis, affectation, biography,
based on true story, based on memoir or autobiography.

17
01:53:20,000 --> 01:53:26,000
The tone is uplifting and emotional.
